## Imagery
- Sentinel-2 cloudless 2016 - https://s2maps.eu by EOX IT Services GmbH (Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data
  2016 & 2017), CC BY 4.0. Layer s2cloudless_3857. Only the 2016 release is used (later releases are CC BY-NC-SA).
  - Globe: zoom 4, assets/world.jpg copied from ../rp_maps (URLs in raw/manifest_world.jsonl).
  - Everest: wide patch zoom 9 (84.9–89.0 E, 26.3–29.7 N), medium zoom 11 (86.2–87.7 E, 27.4–28.6 N),
    detailed zoom 13 (86.70–87.15 E, 27.80–28.17 N).
  - Nyos: wide patch zoom 9 (8.6–12.0 E, 4.9–8.0 N), medium zoom 11 (9.8–10.8 E, 5.95–6.95 N),
    detailed zoom 13 (10.16–10.44 E, 6.30–6.58 N).
  - Modified: colour-graded like the globe (land warmed, a little less saturation); the outer quarter of each wide patch fades
    into the globe texture, the outer tenth of each medium / detailed patch into the patch around it; east of Everest (from 87.19 E) the mosaic
    joins a darker scene: that side is brightened row by row to meet the other (SEAM in tools/fetch_patch.py).
- Elevation: AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen / Tilezen "terrarium" PNG), zoom 9, 11 and 13, https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/
  (sources include SRTM, GMTED, ETOPO1). Everest at true scale (no exaggeration). Nyos relief ×1.6 so the low valleys read
  (the gas layer follows the same scaled surface).
- Every download URL and date is logged in raw/manifest.jsonl (downloaded 2026-11-28).

