## Places (public coordinates) and facts on screen (only what the narration says)
- Everest summit 27.988° N 86.925° E (8 849 m). The pin and the pillar stand on the highest node of the height grid within
  ~1 km (8 746 m on the 75 m grid). Pillar: sea level (0 m, drawn dashed through the mountain) → summit, a tick per km.
  On screen: «Эверест», «почти 9 км» (narration: «почти девять километров»), «уровень моря», «давление ≈ 1/3 / от привычного»
  with a bar of three parts, one lit (narration: «по давлению примерно треть от привычного»).
- Lake Nyos 6.438° N 10.298° E, Cameroon. On screen: «озеро Ньос», «Камерун», «21 августа 1986», «углекислый газ тяжелее
  воздуха». No figures, no people, no text about victims.
- The gas is schematic, not a reconstruction of 1986: tools/gas.py spreads a shallow dense layer from the lake surface over the
  real height grid (it can climb at most 10 m above the lowest ground on its way, starts 45 m above the lake so it spills over
  the lowest point of the rim, moves faster downhill), up to 13 km along the path. The page reveals it by arrival time; soft
  puffs rise from the lake first, then ride the front.

